sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If in an equilateral and equiangular pentagon straight lines subtend two angles are taken in order, then they cut one another in extreme and mean ratio, and their greater segments equal the side of the pentagon.
----
proof:

In the equilateral and equiangular pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} let the straight lines {AC} and {BE}, cutting one another at the point {H}, subtend two angles taken in order, the angles at {A|angBAE} and {B|angABC}.

I say that each of them has been cut in extreme and mean ratio at the point {H}, and their greater segments equal the side of the pentagon.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="260" height="240" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XIII.8 diagram" src="propXIII8.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's pentagon is declared BAEDC; the prose calls it ABCDE and
    // reaches pentT, a faceless twin, since a highlighted random face is
    // raised over the markers (#140). His circle circ (already faceless)
    // is held back until "Circumscribe" and drawn with the compass; the
    // prose reaches it as {ABCDE|circ}.
    //
    // Transparent targets: the five sides, the segments HE, HB, AH, CH of
    // the two diagonals, the triangles ABE, ABC, ABH (explicit ;0 faces),
    // and the circumferences EDC and CB as arcs. CB has no lettered point
    // between its ends, so Xcb (uncoloured) is cut off on the ray from the
    // centre Oc through the midpoint of BC at the radius.
    //
    // Angle markers: the wholes at A and B at 30, the rest at 18 (the two
    // parts at A, and the two angles at H, lie side by side). Colour by
    // size, since the proof shows them equal: BAC = ABE = AEB blue,
    // AHE = EAC green, BAE = ABC = AHB purple. No angle is right.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A and B, free — the given
    // pentagon's side, standing from slide 1. C, D, E, H are derived and
    // listed per slide; nothing to defer.
    var GIVEN = ["BAEDC","pentT","A","B","C","D","E","AB","BC","CD","DE","EA",
                 "AC","BE","H","HE","HB","AH","CH"];
    var ANG   = GIVEN.concat(["angBAE","angABC"]);
    var CIRC  = ANG.concat(["circ","ABE","ABC","ABH"]);
    var BAC   = CIRC.concat(["angBAC","angABE"]);
    var AHE   = BAC.concat(["angAHE"]);
    var EAC   = AHE.concat(["angEAC","arcEDC","arcCB"]);
    var AEB   = EAC.concat(["angAEB"]);
    var AHB   = AEB.concat(["angAHB"]);
